# Implementation Documentation Reminder

When making **significant changes** to services, controllers, repositories, or mappers, check whether implementation docs need updating.

## When to act

- New service or controller (new CRUD feature)
- Major refactor of business logic in a service implementation
- New repository with custom queries or specifications
- Changes to how data flows between layers (controller → service → repository)
- New integration with external systems (S3, email, etc.)

## When NOT to act

- Minor bug fixes or adding a field to an existing DTO
- Small query adjustments
- Logging or error message changes

## What to do

1. Check `docs/implementation/` for an existing doc covering this feature area
2. If one exists, update it with the new implementation details
3. If none exists and the change introduces a new feature or pattern, create a new implementation doc
4. Name files as `kebab-case.md` in the appropriate domain subfolder
5. Update `docs/README.md` index with a link to the new doc

## Implementation doc should cover

- What was built and why
- Key classes and their responsibilities
- API endpoints (method, path, request/response shapes)
- Database tables involved and relationships
- Any non-obvious patterns, workarounds, or business rules
- Related architecture decisions (link to ADR if applicable)

## Ask the user

> "This adds/changes [feature area] implementation. Should I create/update an implementation doc in `docs/implementation/`?"
